[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6001259685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6001259685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6001259685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZbP0pQ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T19:09:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T19:09:49Z","body":"While testing this PR, I noticed that changing the game speed to run slower via the toolbar takes a moment to take effect, while changing it to go faster happens quicker.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6001259685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6010138944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6010138944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6010138944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZjtxQA","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T05:41:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T06:05:03Z","body":"> While testing this PR, I noticed that changing the game speed to run slower via the toolbar takes a moment to take effect, while changing it to go faster happens quicker.\r\n\r\nIt's interesting, the transition does look as though it could be slightly different when going slower. I compared with the old system, but the old system was very glitchy on my system so hard to see. I'll do some frame captures to see over a few frames and compare.\r\n\r\nThe logic is sound in the PR, so if something is causing a small glitch there, it's likely doing something \"naughty\", like caching time, accessing outside our system (e.g. third party code) or another line that needs changing to `get_ticks_usec_raw()` (am expecting a couple of those - it could literally be as simple as the running game receiving the command from the editor later, because of a slower read loop where it should be using raw). Especially any glitch occurring over more than a single frame duration is likely a special case.\r\n\r\nIt's no biggie but I'll see if I can track it down, don't think it should be anything to worry about.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a77438b-c707-4708-bfdc-0883c8b99deb\r\n\r\nSo far in the screen cap I'm not noticing anything glitchy, so it's suggestive it could just be a changing delay from editor -> running game. But I'll try a 3d game.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/622bb069-92a0-4d20-8e51-8ccd4bb14f37\r\n\r\nYeah the screencaps seem to confirm - this seems purely down to a change in the communication rate between the Godot IDE and the running game, and something in there (on the game side) probably would benefit from using `get_ticks_usec_raw()` instead of `get_ticks_usec()`. I'll see if I can work it out, there's probably a delay loop somewhere in the network code or something.\r\n\r\nUPDATE: Oh yeah there's a few places in the networking calling `get_ticks_msec()` and I didn't grep for those, that passes through to the `get_ticks_usec()` so I'll change them to the raw version, possibly add a `get_ticks_msec_raw()` to make that easier. :+1: \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6010138944/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6010779951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6010779951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6010779951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZkU5Lw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T06:33:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T06:33:47Z","body":"Ok try that, I've added `get_ticks_msec_raw()` and called it from a few places in the audio and networking. As far as I can see there's a slight delay between clicking the speed in the editor and it being reflected in the running game, but the delay now seems constant at different game speeds.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6010779951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012119258","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6012119258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6012119258,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZlmo2g","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:08:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T08:13:23Z","body":"I'm not really sure I fully understand this.\r\n\r\nThe PR references \"Wall Clock\" multiple times, but wall clock is non-monotonic and can jump by minutes (forward or backward) after a NTP sync (wall clock is what the user see in the OS bar).\r\n\r\nIn practice, \"Wall Clock\" doesn't really have a correlation with time passing, it can only be used to know what time point a user is currently seeing from the OS.\r\n\r\nAm I missing something here?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012119258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012192077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6012192077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6012192077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZlrFTQ","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:13:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T08:14:45Z","body":"> Am I missing something here?\r\n\r\nNaming convention causing confusion with OS call?\r\nWe could name this something different to differentiate if it causes confusion.\r\n\r\nSuggestions welcome! :smile: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012192077/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012202339","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6012202339","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6012202339,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZlrtYw","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:14:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T08:14:21Z","body":"> Naming convention causing confusion with OS call?\r\n> We could name this something different to differentiate if it causes confusion.\r\n\r\nYeah, I would really prefer using a different naming here, because wall clock is very confusing IMO","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012202339/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012315581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6012315581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6012315581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZlynvQ","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:21:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T08:21:53Z","body":"> Suggestions welcome! 😄\r\n\r\nMaybe `game_clock`? `engine_clock`?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012315581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012375458","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6012375458","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6012375458,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZl2Rog","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T08:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T13:29:42Z","body":"I think we already have a `game_time_scale` (which works underneath this level).\r\n\r\nSo maybe as you say `engine_clock` or even `master_clock` might be better.\r\n\r\nActually I meant to mention, the other option is to add an `enum` to the existing `set_time_scale` and default it to the old game scale for backward compatibility, and add a new enum member for the master / engine clock.\r\n\r\nThere's no particular reason these need to be separate functions, and it's possible we might want to add a third time_scaling method specifically for bullet time (and because the existing `game_time_scale` isn't super useful in terms of Q and A, but removing it completely would be breaking compatibility).\r\n\r\nUPDATE:\r\nRenamed to \"primary_time_scale\". I would have preferred \"master\" but that can be a bit politically sensitive.\r\n\r\nI did evaluate changing to an `enum` and reusing the existing `set_time_scale` on `Engine`, that would have introduced a dependency to OS from Engine that didn't exist so far, which wouldn't have been ideal.\r\n\r\nI did also consider future proofing the `OS` version by having a timescale enum with `primary` as the only member, but it seemed overkill as we are only likely to introduce one more `bullet` version, and being able to e.g. call the `Engine::set_time_scale()` _from_ the OS version would have been even more confusing I suspect.\r\n\r\nAnd indeed we may decide not to bind the primary time scale in the long run, and have it just for the editor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6012375458/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6020623763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123955#issuecomment-6020623763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123955","id":6020623763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZtttkw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T16:21:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T09:23:37Z","body":"Great! I've asked @Ivorforce if he gets a chance to look at the atomics etc, or anyone else is welcome to check, as it's very easy to get wrong.. e.g. @RandomShaper , @NoctemCat , anyone familiar with atomics.\r\n\r\n_Just repushed using a local alias for `_primary_clock` in the functions, to make them easier to read._\r\n\r\nIt might be an idea to schedule this for 4.9 actually if we are in feature freeze (depending how many betas there will be), as I'm positive I'll have missed the odd place in the audio / network which needs swapping to use `get_ticks_usec_raw()`, and we won't know without testing in the wild where the last pesky ones are.\r\n\r\nHowever there's also the 3.x version with the same internals #123978 so reviews here are relevant to both, and I'm keen to that in sooner for 3.7 dev 2 if possible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6020623763/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]